Z||000006||Brandon86SE||09-21-2001||08:41 PM||||NO!  It does not make sense, and neither is it supposed to!  We are talking about a teenaged girl here, they don't make sense, and if you try to understand, you'll drive yourself batty!  I'm not getting into it right now, but I put up with that kind of talk for 4 months very recently!!!!  I'm much happier now working on my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, and hanging out with my friends, than having to try and understand what was going on, and try to decipher how each little thing that happens affects the whole situation.  WAY TOO MUCH WORK!!!!!  You have a Fiero, be happy, and content with that!  Then, if something all of a sudden comes up, then "hurrah!".  But, in my opinion, there's no reason to put up with talk like that.<P>Best of luck (to you, and all of us single, confused young males),<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000007||dennis_6||09-21-2001||11:12 PM||||I agree with you Brandon86SE.<BR>My ex-fiance who I had been dating for over three years in the same day went house shoppig with me and about died over a brick ranch on 5 acres and then broke off our relationship that evening for no reason whatsoever. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">   She had just mysteriously decided we were not compatible.  Note I was with her all day and I have been faithful the whole relationship.  So go figure.  I have had alot of time to mess with my Fiero since! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>P.S. I have an 86 SE too. ||||reg||10
