Z||000011||FieroHeather||09-22-2001||12:14 AM||||Here's the female perspective on the whole thing:<P>She is indecisive, and is not too sure of herself.  She is waiting for you to help make decisions for her and take charge somewhat of what the relationship should be--not just asking her questions about what could be.<P>She is being honest with you about one of her weaknesses: Flirting.  It also means that she has a weakness for "the game" and probably will not be positive 'committed girlfriend' material.  Give her a few years and she may grow out of it.<P>But dont go chasing after her dude...you could get burned in the end, big time.  You should definitely be up front with her.  If she is not into being comitted to you in such a simple way of being a gf/bf, then she probably wont be too keen on future relationship stuff.  Look for females who show signs of faithfulness and are currently not hooked up with anyone--they make the BEST gf's.  <P>The best predictor of future behavior is past behavior (from Dr. Phil).  As another saying goes: Once a cheater (flirter), always a cheater.  Gotta strive to find someone who's not going to play games with ya dude.  There's lots of us females out there that are worth waiting for  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Brandon86SE||09-22-2001||12:31 AM||||Heather - Are you single?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  jj  Besides, even though you're in Canada, Barrie is a long ways from Calgary!<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||09-22-2001||02:05 AM||||O.K. - upon re-reading my statement up there, my comment of "nailing her and finding someone else" was a bit too harsh. I would like to soften a bit of the harshness of that statement.<P>For some women (in my experience), things need to progress (in a consensual manner) to that point (that of deciding whether or not to pursue a physical relationship) for them to be able to make up their minds about whether or not they wish to pursue the other facets of the relationship. It was this situation that I was referring to when I (rather crudely) said "Nail her if she'll let you"... if the two of you agree to it, then for some people, it clarifies things. (Admittedly, for some others, it can muddy the waters even further, but at this point, it is usually a given that the guy wants to have sex, so the actual decision is truly up to the woman. Having to actually make the decision usually seems to bring other questions she may have into better focus as well, even if the decision about sex is 'no'.)<P>For heaven's sake, don't rush to this issue in order to attempt to clarify things if the two of you are not ready for it... this advice is better considered if the two of you are close to or at that stage in the relationship already. <P>Just my two cents as they have been learned in my experience...<P>EDIT - typos<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 09-22-2001).]||||reg||1
